{
    "version": "1.9.11",
    "changelog": "Six things. (1) Paired objects: where one road exists as two runs (split by a crossing road, or the two sides of a median stretch), the runs are now ONE piece in the editor whenever the data marks them with a shared 'grp' value \u2014 clicking any run selects the whole object, the Pieces panel lists it as one entry naming every run, and Delete removes the whole object through the usual framed check. Merge and Join leave paired objects alone. Where no grp marks exist, nothing changes. (2) Join takes chains: select 3 or more pieces and Join makes them one road, forming every space between them straight or curved as their ends run. Merge still takes exactly 2. Shift+click adds a piece at any time; Ctrl+click takes one piece out. (3) Lasso: hold Shift and drag a line that loops back to its start \u2014 every piece inside is added to the selection (the lasso only selects; you then choose what to do). (4) Draw works: with Draw on, dragging lays a new road and panning is off; let go to add it, saved like any edit. (5) The editor opens with no tool armed, and zone or building jumps arm nothing either. (6) Selecting a piece now wakes the 3D still pane, framed on the exact spot you clicked at street level \u2014 it no longer stays black after selecting.",
